{
  "timestamp": "2026-07-30T14:25:03Z",
  "title": "Chapters roster refresh and Founders & AI communities",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "Project context: We need to modernize the https://www.harvardintech.com/ website from the outside. The site was built with a no-code product so we need to faithfully reproduce it using modern technologies and host it as a GitHub pages website. It also needs a CRM that can be run locally or, ideally also in the cloud via GitHub pages as well (protected with a password and/or GitHub OAuth). Can we dig into this?",
  "description": "The chapter roster is now Boston & Cambridge, DC and DMV Area, London, New York City, Seattle / Pacific Northwest and SF & Bay Area: SF is a new chapter page, Seattle and DC were relabelled, and the roster sorts alphabetically because every entry's numeric `order` pin was removed rather than renumbered — `order` stays in the schema as an optional pin, so adding a chapter no longer means editing the others. Founders and AI became real pages at /communities/<slug>, rendered through the same ChapterPage shell as a chapter and derived into the Communities menu; the asymmetry with Chapters is deliberate — Chapters is a group the layout injects whole, while Communities already belongs to an editor in nav.json, so derived items join its children behind the hand-authored WhatsApp link. Events join a community through the same `chapter` tag chapters use, so editors learn no second field, and the shared page components took a `name` prop in place of `city` since they now render both kinds.\n\nThree fixes fell out of the work rather than the plan. The seed adapter serialized nested `leads`/`links` rows as the literal text `[object Object]`, so any scenario seeding them rendered an Astro schema error instead of the page — its YAML writer now emits block maps, which is what makes the Founders scenario possible at all. The homepage's \"5 Global chapters\" stat and the hero carousel's hard-coded city list had both gone stale against the collection. And CMS_SETUP.md still documented order-field menu sorting and a chapters-only event tag.\n\nOne limitation worth recording: on the isolated PrimaryNav route a scenario `hover`/`click` interaction does not survive the screenshot (it reports `interactionEffect: none`), so the pre-existing \"Derived Chapters\" scenario has always captured a closed menu despite its description. The new Communities scenario therefore uses its own isolation route that pins the panel open, rather than relying on an interaction that silently captures nothing.",
